{"title":"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_23\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 23</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Simpler)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Simpler)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_23\">Problem 23</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 23\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/8/a9874ea56cf8fec1bd246793224fbcfaad17ab3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> lie on a line, in that order, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a427387ff6212e24b2c3bf3ce692b2e62d50a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = CD$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/f/d5fb59fff6b6968adfa1e4b3d06a609a2a8af375.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is not on the line, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/2/102f733a99ce9d33fabdd5e5ba7ad1187a5565bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE = CE = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"14\" />. The perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18167d788fd698322ba516cf8bfdba2c931fa17d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AED$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is twice the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97dd577dd14751b09771a1c83d880f5142b86181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BEC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970138dce96b3f6aea2cf911e99c04d13efd7c70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 15/2 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 17/2 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 9 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 19/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"411\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we draw an altitude to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let it intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97dd577dd14751b09771a1c83d880f5142b86181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BEC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles, we immediately get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d2f7d331088511a83b2c800453f3bd86ee9a0b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB=MC=6$\" width=\"125\" height=\"12\" />, so the altitude is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/6/716b45f37eb66b0c165d0afcc2b8f2b596323c5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=CD=x$\" width=\"116\" height=\"13\" />. Using the Pythagorean Theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e15c6bc4d2a7e91a9fb5b77871d857aec0efd65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EMA$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" />, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/7/677fcc00cebc0f29e58a5829993c6e4ff71e2fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=\\sqrt{x^2+12x+100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />. From symmetry, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f56db1894644727c2ccb738ec3ecb95aa385a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=\\sqrt{x^2+12x+100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"188\" height=\"18\" /> as well. Now, we use the fact that the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/1/18167d788fd698322ba516cf8bfdba2c931fa17d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AED$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is twice the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97dd577dd14751b09771a1c83d880f5142b86181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BEC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b79ebfcff1a86b654fef6c643e2b188609e7c04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(0.25 cm);  pair A, B, C, D, E, M;  A = (0,0); B = (9,0); C = (21,0); D = (30,0); E = (15,-8); M = (15,0);  draw(A--D--E--cycle); draw(B--E); draw(M--E); draw(C--E);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, N); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, N); label(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, S); label(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, N); [/asy]\" width=\"375\" height=\"142\" />\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23f25cc6c4e5af10ac42e1f9e6fec7d0c2ddb1ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt{x^2+12x+100}+2x+12=2(32)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"288\" height=\"21\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/5806709b2f5a7417059b93c3e19e403c696b8109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{x^2+12x+100}=26-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" />. Squaring both sides, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4d505eea4d1e0c93f8e6037002a2fca4a55edb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+12x+100=676-52x+x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"259\" height=\"16\" /> which nicely rearranges into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/e/b0e1fe06a2c576cfbe4101f4fecee249b175be90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64x=576\\rightarrow{x=9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"151\" height=\"13\" />. Hence, AB is 9 so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc93afd012d6af697c4fae71d14de49f021d78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"37\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Simpler.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Simpler)\">Solution 2 (Simpler)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Simpler)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f6f7cd16a47f33bebcf3fc361eeb808b630504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC.$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/2/6d2f7d331088511a83b2c800453f3bd86ee9a0b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB=MC=6$\" width=\"125\" height=\"12\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97dd577dd14751b09771a1c83d880f5142b86181.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BEC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles. By the Pythagorean triple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/0514b5c78bcf23d88fc697a05a66250517dc5519.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(6,8,10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> the altitude is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/1/bb13a1ea7b9fd6892ebe9599c3587aa68288c873.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/d/39de39884ea5612d1f0520e299a01fefd9daf2f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8,15,17)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> is the only primitive Pythagorean triple with leg <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12a9fb4c5b23667e57f28d844ad99715f18ba3fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> we test <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd49bc521eb85bea9c002a0546e75dddd2cd6ca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=DE=17,AM=DM=15.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"271\" height=\"16\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba496014cbed53522ce712d6a5d79c0c429efa16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(10+10+12)=(17+17+2\\cdot 15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"280\" height=\"18\" /> this works, giving us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/1/5f185a7edea1ca0474f38a209b56d4827e354c23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=15-6=\\boxed{\\text{(D)}\\ 9}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"181\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~dolphin7\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HJkfO6vuIwg\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HJkfO6vuIwg</a>  ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A\">2002 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2002 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017060118\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 301/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7344/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.780      1 -total\n 60.24%    7.698      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.80%    4.959      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7495:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017060118 and revision id 264230. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}